# Gable roof + Y-truss

When adding or editing an open-gable **standing-seam roof** with a **Y-truss** (chord + king post + two angled arms):

**Follow:** `docs/agent-gable-y-truss-roof.md` (full recipe, formulas, anti-patterns, PH reference numbers).

## Hard rules (summary)

- Two items: `procedural:phroof:W:H:D:HEX` and `procedural:ytruss:CHORD:ARM_LEN:THICK:HEX`
- Truss members all white (`f5f5f4`) unless Owner says otherwise
- Chord at **plate/eave**, span ≈ post outer−inset — never full-span mid-attic (punches slopes)
- `ARM_LEN = (ridgeY − tipMargin − chordTop) / cos(40°)`; tips under ridge
- Gable face: rotate so chord lies in the open gable plane (`π/2` for east gable on PH)
- `ypos` is chord **center** (loader keeps bbox mid on chord — do not fight this)
- Save via `POST /api/plans` merge; Reload → 3D; verify no poke-through
